GREEDY ALGORITHMS

Definition: Make the best local choice at each step without normally revisiting previous choices.

Properties: Greedy-choice property and optimal substructure.

Workflow:
    Understand objective
    identify greedy rule
    sort/use data structure
    select valid candidate
    update state
    prove correctness
    analyze complexity

Important patterns:
    Activity Selection:
        sort by finish time;
        select if start >= lastFinish.

    Fractional Knapsack:
        sort by value/weight descending;
        take full items or a fraction.

    Job Sequencing:
        sort by profit descending;
        schedule in the latest free slot before deadline.

    Coin Change:
        largest coin first is not always optimal for arbitrary denominations.

    Kruskal: choose the cheapest safe edge.

    Dijkstra:
        choose the nearest unsettled vertex;
        requires non-negative edge weights.

Complexity:
    sorting + scan O(n log n);
    scan O(n);
    heap operation O(log n).

Golden rule:
    A locally best choice is not necessarily globally optimal;
    justify the greedy rule.